+Proposed HAL change (ws052-p016, NOT applied, needs the user's approval before any implementation).
+Reads the processor's residency counter of a low-power idle state that the firmware's LPIT names in
+functional fixed hardware (on the Latitude 5330: LPIT state 0, MSR 0x632, the package C10 residency).
+
+--- a/include/hal/hal.h
++++ b/include/hal/hal.h
+@@ -586,6 +586,26 @@
+ 	uint64_t *counter,
+ 	uint64_t *freq_hz);
+ 
++/*
++ * Read a processor's residency counter of a low-power idle state.
++ *
++ * address is the address field of the counter's generic address in the
++ * firmware's low-power idle table when its address space is functional
++ * fixed hardware (on amd64 the number of a model-specific register).  The
++ * HAL reads only the counters it knows to count the residency of an idle
++ * state of the processor package (on amd64 the package C-state residency
++ * registers) and reports HAL_ERR_UNSUPPORTED for any other address, and
++ * on every architecture without such counters.  On HAL_OK, value is the
++ * counter as the current CPU reads it (a package's counter is the same on
++ * each of its CPUs) and freq_hz the frequency it counts at, nonzero.
++ * It may be called from any thread with interrupts enabled or not, and
++ * changes nothing.
++ */
++int
++hal_cpu_read_residency_counter(
++	uint64_t address,
++	uint64_t *value,
++	uint64_t *freq_hz);
+ 
